.TH VEZ.CONF 5 "2026" "vez" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
vez.conf \- configuration file for vez
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/vez/vez.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
vez reads its main configuration from a dnf.conf compatible file, under
a single
.B [main]
section. Only the options listed below are recognized; any other dnf.conf
option is accepted and ignored. Command line flags always take
precedence over a value set here, which in turn takes precedence over
vez's own built in default.
.PP
See
.BR dnf.conf (5)
for background on the file format and on options this file shares with
dnf.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B cachedir\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Directory where downloaded .rpm files are cached before install.
Default: /var/cache/vez.
.TP
.B reposdir\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Directory of dnf/yum style .repo files. Default: /etc/yum.repos.d.
.TP
.B keepcache\fR=\fI0|1\fR
Whether to keep downloaded packages in the cache after a successful
install. Default: 0.
.TP
.B assumeyes\fR=\fI0|1\fR
Assume "yes" to any prompt. Default: 0.
.TP
.B assumeno\fR=\fI0|1\fR
Assume "no" to any prompt. Default: 0.
.TP
.B gpgcheck\fR=\fI0|1\fR
Verify package GPG signatures. Default: 1.
.TP
.B best\fR=\fI0|1\fR
Require the newest available version to resolve cleanly, rather than
silently falling back to an older one. Default: 1.
.TP
.B exclude\fR=\fIPATTERN[,PATTERN...]\fR
Exclude matching packages (glob capable) from consideration in every
run, unless overridden on the command line or turned off with
disable_excludes.
.TP
.B includepkgs\fR=\fIPATTERN[,PATTERN...]\fR
Restrict consideration to only matching packages.
.TP
.B disable_excludes\fR=\fImain|*\fR
Disable the exclude= filtering above for this system.
.TP
.B metadata_expire\fR=\fISECONDS\fR
How long cached repo metadata stays valid before vez refreshes it.
Default: 172800 (two days).
.TP
.B retries\fR=\fIN\fR
Number of times to retry a failed download or metadata fetch. Default:
10.
.TP
.B timeout\fR=\fISECONDS\fR
Stall timeout: abort a download if no data arrives for this long.
Default: 30.
.TP
.B max_parallel_downloads\fR=\fIN\fR
Maximum number of packages to download at once. Default: 3.
.TP
.B skip_if_unavailable\fR=\fI0|1\fR
Continue past a repo whose metadata can't be fetched instead of
failing. Default: 0.
.TP
.B clean_requirements_on_remove\fR=\fI0|1\fR
Whether removing a package also removes its now unneeded
dependency only packages. Default: 1.
.TP
.B installroot\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Operate against an alternate root instead of the real /. Default: /.
.TP
.B installonlypkgs\fR=\fIPATTERN[,PATTERN...]\fR
Packages (like the kernel) that install side by side across versions
instead of replacing the previous build.
.TP
.B protected_packages\fR=\fINAME[,NAME...]\fR
Packages that vez refuses to remove, in addition to its own always
protected names.
.TP
.B install_weak_deps\fR=\fI0|1\fR
Whether to pull in weak dependencies (Recommends) when resolving a
transaction.
.TP
.B multilib_policy\fR=\fIbest|all\fR
Whether to install only the best matching architecture build of a
package, or every distinct architecture build side by side.
.TP
.B obsoletes\fR=\fI0|1\fR
Whether package obsoletes are honored during resolution.
.TP
.B skip_broken\fR=\fI0|1\fR
If the full requested install set can't be resolved together, drop
whichever names are responsible and proceed with the rest.
.TP
.B sslverify\fR=\fI0|1\fR
Verify TLS certificates when talking to repos. Default: 1. Setting this
to 0 is an escape hatch for a repo behind a broken or self signed
certificate chain and should not be used otherwise.
.TP
.B proxy\fR=\fIURL\fR
Proxy URL used for all repo requests.
.TP
.B proxy_username\fR=\fIUSER\fR
.TQ
.B proxy_password\fR=\fIPASSWORD\fR
Credentials for the configured proxy.
.TP
.B username\fR=\fIUSER\fR
.TQ
.B password\fR=\fIPASSWORD\fR
Default basic auth credentials sent with every repo request.
.TP
.B ip_resolve\fR=\fI4|6|ipv4|ipv6\fR
Restrict repo requests to one IP address family.
.TP
.B user_agent\fR=\fISTRING\fR
Override the User\-Agent header sent with repo requests.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/vez/vez.conf
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vez (1),
.BR dnf.conf (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Svara project.
